cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hpsc-integrity: chromosome-arm screening of human pluripotent stem cell RNA-seq (research prototype)"
type: software
version: 0.0.5
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jbaileyi/hpsc-integrity"
authors:
  - given-names: Bailey
    family-names: Johnson
abstract: >-
  Python package and CLI that combines expression-based chromosome-arm tiers with allelic-imbalance
  evidence from heterozygous SNPs in bulk RNA-seq of human pluripotent stem cells. Validated in-sample on five
  hESC lines and checked for specificity on 12 held-out HipSci lines; sensitivity and clone-fraction accuracy
  are not validated on held-out data. See the README for limitations.
keywords:
  - pluripotent stem cells
  - RNA-seq
  - copy number
  - allelic imbalance
  - karyotype
